+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+When a GraphHelm-bound session ends, the host hook (`plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py`) POSTs an
+`agent_session_ended` signal to the Runtime with the actor identity in `X-GraphHelm-Actor` (a
+composite `{host}-session-{session}` id) but nothing carrying the host session id itself. The
+Runtime already parses, validates, and persists an `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header into its
+structured presence record, so the hook's end request currently leaves that record without a
+session id even though the hook has one and validates it.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- The SessionEnd hook's `POST /v1/executions/{executionId}/signal` request sends the validated
+  host session id (the hook payload `session_id`, cross-checked against `GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID`
+  when that environment binding is set) in the `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header, alongside the
+  existing `X-GraphHelm-Actor`, `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Type`, and `Idempotency-Key` headers.
+- The existing end-request contract test in `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py`
+  (`test_end_posts_an_attributed_idempotent_observation_without_success_claim`) is extended to
+  assert that the header is present with the correct value.
+- Explicitly unchanged, per the request: no new header-building helper is added (the header is a
+  single entry in the literal headers dict at the existing call site), the SessionStart/briefing
+  request gains no header, the signal body and idempotency key are untouched, and the hook's
+  other tests must stay green.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `session-hook-signals`: Wire contract for the `agent_session_ended` signal the GraphHelm host
+  hooks deliver to the Runtime on SessionEnd, including the actor attribution headers carried by
+  that request. No spec for this behavior exists under `openspec/specs/` yet (verified empty), so
+  this delta establishes it.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+<!-- none: no existing specs under openspec/specs/ -->
+
+## Impact
+
+- Code: `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/session_hook.py` — the header dict in `_end_impl`'s `request(...)`
+  call site (one entry). Tests: `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_session_hook.py` — one assertion
+  added to the existing end-request test.
+- Runtime (Rust): no change needed — `apps/cli/src/commands/serve/mod.rs` already reads and
+  validates `x-graphhelm-actor-session` (visible ASCII, ≤128 chars, not blank). The hook's own
+  session validation (`ID` regex) is stricter than every Runtime door check, so a session the hook
+  accepts always satisfies the Runtime.
+- No new dependencies, no changed endpoints, no new headers on the start/briefing request, no
+  change to the signal body, state file format, or idempotency key. Retried end deliveries resend
+  the same signal bytes with the same headers.
