+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Defines the wire contract for the `agent_session_ended` signal that GraphHelm host hooks deliver to the Runtime when a bound session ends, including the actor-attribution headers the end request must carry so the Runtime's structured presence record receives the host session id.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: End request carries the host session id
+On SessionEnd of a bound session, the hook's signal POST to the Runtime SHALL include an `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header carrying the validated host session id (the payload `session_id`, which must equal `GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID` when set), alongside the existing actor, actor-type, and idempotency headers. The value SHALL satisfy the Runtime's door rules (visible ASCII, at most 128 characters, not blank); the header SHALL NOT alter the signal body or idempotency key.
+
+#### Scenario: Bound session end delivers the session header
+- **WHEN** a hook bound to an execution receives a valid `SessionEnd` payload with `session_id` "session-123" and no `GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID` override
+- **THEN** the POSTed signal request carries `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session: session-123` in addition to the actor, actor-type, and idempotency headers
+- **AND** the signal body and idempotency key are unchanged from before this requirement
+
+#### Scenario: Environment-pinned session wins over a mismatching payload
+- **WHEN** `GRAPHHELM_SESSION_ID` is set to a value different from the payload `session_id`
+- **THEN** the hook treats the run as unobserved without sending any request, so no end request ever carries a session header that disagrees with the pinned binding
+
+### Requirement: Retried end deliveries repeat the same session header
+A retried delivery of the same session-end signal SHALL resend the identical `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` value together with the identical signal bytes and idempotency key, so the Runtime attributes every attempt of one logical delivery to the same host session.
+
+#### Scenario: Retry after a refused response keeps the header
+- **WHEN** the first end POST is refused by the Runtime and the hook later retries the pending delivery
+- **THEN** the retry sends the same signal body, the same `Idempotency-Key`, and the same `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` value as the first attempt
+
+### Requirement: Start and briefing requests are unchanged
+The SessionStart path (including its live briefing GET) SHALL NOT send an `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header, and its other headers and observable behavior SHALL remain exactly as defined before this change.
+
+#### Scenario: Briefing GET carries no session header
+- **WHEN** a bound SessionStart fetches the live briefing from the Runtime
+- **THEN** the GET request carries its existing headers only and no `X-GraphHelm-Actor-Session` header
